    "analysis": "The official task is counting monotone paths around blocked cells. The supplied baseline performs O(N²) work and allocates O(N²) blocked-cell storage despite potentially sparse obstacles. Sparse path-count subtraction can reduce work to O(M²), but the stated bound does not ensure that is affordable; a compact rolling-row dense method provides a distinct alternative. The only automatic measurement is a valid baseline (0.080673 s mean, score 0.5, four correctness cases); there are no candidate measurements, so gains must be established experimentally."
